  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Description:\nSDK appears to think you're building for a different platform (e.g. Android when project is set to PC) when that platform's overrides tab is open in a texture's Import Settings.\nSDK Version Date: 2021.08.11.15.16\nUnity version: 2019.4.29f1\nRepro Steps: In a SDK3 project targeting the PC platform, build a world that is larger than 50MB and leave the SDK's Builder tab open. Then, click on a Texture, and in the Inspector, click on the tab with the Android icon. Next, click anywhere inside the SDK window.\nExpected: The SDK window does not change state.\nActual: The over-50MB-limit warning for Android appears, and building the world is prevented by a filesize warning.\nI have noticed this occurring in both 2018 and 2019 for a few months. To revert the SDK to thinking we're on PC again, you have to click the PC tab in the Texture Importer, then click back into the SDK window. Otherwise, the wrong platform is identified even after the texture is deselected.\nLink to video: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ubt5W2OzA1MfXYHYOrXZeKB7KTIxg7dg/view?usp=sharing",
